# Project Defaults

## Tech Stack

- Astro 5.x, Tailwind 4, TypeScript (strict), pnpm
- ESLint + Prettier (with astro, tailwindcss, jsx-a11y plugins)
- astro-icon for icons

## Code Quality

```bash
pnpm prettier --write .    # Format
pnpm eslint . --fix        # Lint
```

## File Structure

```
src/
├── assets/        # Images (imported as modules)
├── components/    # All components (PascalCase.astro)
├── layouts/       # Page wrappers
├── pages/         # Routes
├── styles/        # global.css, fonts.css
└── schemas/       # Zod validation (if using forms)
public/            # Static assets (favicons, robots.txt)
```

## Imports

- Always use path aliases, never relative imports
- Available: `@components`, `@layouts`, `@pages`, `@assets`, `@styles`, `@schemas`, `@public`

**Order within files:**

1. Framework (`astro:*`, `astro-icon/components`)
2. Components (`@components/*`, `@layouts/*`)
3. Assets (`@assets/*`)
4. Schemas/utilities (`@schemas/*`)
5. Types (`import type` from `astro/types`)

## Component Structure Order

1. Imports
2. Type definitions (`type Props = {...}`)
3. Props destructuring
4. Data fetching
5. Computed values
6. Template
7. `<style>` (if needed)
8. `<script>` (if needed)

## TypeScript

- Use `type`, never `interface`
- Extend HTML attributes: `type Props = HTMLAttributes<'button'> & {...}`
- Let TypeScript infer return types
- Co-locate types with usage (no central `types/` folder)

## Tailwind

- Write classes inline in template only (Prettier plugin won't sort frontmatter variables)
- Use `class:list` for conditionals

```astro
<!-- ✓ Inline classes with class:list -->
<button
  class:list={[
    'px-4 py-2 text-white',
    variant === 'primary' && 'bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600',
    variant === 'secondary' && 'bg-gray-500 hover:bg-gray-600',
  ]}
>
  <slot />
</button>

<!-- ✗ Classes in frontmatter variables -->
```

## Styles Setup

- `src/styles/global.css`: imports fonts.css + tailwindcss
- `src/styles/fonts.css`: @import for external, @font-face for local fonts
